      "headline": "Flood Advisory issued November 19 at 2:02PM PST until November 19 at 2:45PM PST by NWS San Diego CA",
      "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.\n\n* WHERE...Riverside County in southern California...\nSan Bernardino County in southern California...\n\n* WHEN...Until 245 PM PST.\n\n* IMPACTS...Rises in small streams and normally dry arroyos. Ponding\nof water in urban or other areas is occurring or is imminent.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 201 PM PST, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nheavy rain. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area. Between 0.5 and 1.25 inches of rain\nhave fallen.\n- Additional rainfall amounts up to 0.5 inches are expected over\nthe area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nRiverside, San Bernardino, Fontana, Moreno Valley, Corona,\nRialto, Redlands, Lake Elsinore and Yucaipa.\n- https://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
      "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nIn hilly terrain there are hundreds of low water crossings which are\npotentially dangerous in heavy rain. Do not attempt to cross flooded\nroads. Find an alternate route. Minor rockfalls are possible.",
